among the crown makers.","Feed the class fish before joining a game.","Find a spare ruler before drawing a chart.","Give a beginning player a cue for their own part.","Hang bags on hooks to leave reading seats free.","Keep clean paper pieces for another group to use.","Keep the magnifier on its labelled shelf.","Look inside a bag before deciding it is empty.","Make name labels so visitors can identify display pictures.","Move a plant into another pot when its pot breaks.","Move one light panel to try a scenery job.","Name a door and its nearby landmark for a visitor.","Name an object and its shelf when asking for it.","Offer a number of decorations you have time to finish.","Practise a game’s goal with a child who is new.","Put a large model on a table away from a doorway.","Put game counters back in their own game box.","Put the event banner beside your bag the night before.","Repair a loose wheel before decorating a working cart.","Restore a scattered board before asking for another game.","Share the weight when a crate is too heavy to lift.","Show a new pupil what a classroom signal means.","Show how to find an edge before returning puzzle pieces.","Sort scattered score cards into their proper order.","Start runners from the same line when comparing speed.","Take short turns when two players share a drum.","Tell the referee when a recorded score needs changing.","Try a short shaker rhythm before joining a song.","Use the same cup when comparing how much jugs hold.","Wait until the bottom of a slide is clear.","a doorway used by a carrier","a fold along the edge of paper","a folded blanket used for warmth","a handle for carrying a bottle","a metal hook at the end of a rope","a person teaching a class","a place where buses stop for passengers","a player who guards the goal","a pocket sewn onto some trousers","a printed address on an envelope","a sandy place beside the sea","a set of goalposts for a game","a television screen","a wooden handle on a hammer","a written list of party snacks","big","carrying the hoop","checking the address","checking the clock","checking the score","choosing a book","choosing a chair","choosing a pear","choosing a spoon","choosing the dish","clipping up the plan","closing the atlas","closing the box","closing the drawer","closing the shade","closing the window","colouring the picture","colourless","counting her coins","counting the birds","counting the butterflies","counting the pots","counting the tickets","counting the visitors","covering the clay","crossing the bridge","disconnected","drawing a line","drawing the labels","drawing the moon","drinking water","drying her shoes","fetching the register","filling his bottle","filling the jug","filling the trough","fin","finding the tape","folding her scarf","folding the cloth","folding the map","folding the napkins","folding the rag","greeting the host","handing over his ticket","hanging his coat","hanging up his helmet","hanging up the keys","harmless","humming the song","leaving her bag","lifting her basket","lifting the magnet","measuring the card","miscounted","moving the blanket","moving the stool","moving the vase","opening the curtain","opening the packet","opening the tin","packing her cup","packing his notebook","passing out the shakers","pen","photographing the jetty","pinning on a badge","putting away his hat","putting down the bag","putting his bag on the bench","putting on a coat","putting on his hat","putting out the menus","putting the bear on the bed","reading his ticket","reading the sign","refilled","rib","ringing the bell","ringing the buzzer","rob","rolling in the bike","rotating the globe","setting out the chairs","setting the timer","sewing the puppet’s hat","sharpening his pencil","smoothing the bowl","sorting the cards","stacking the cards","stacking the cushions","stopping the fan","stroking the cat","sum","switching on the torch","taking a bow","testing the microphone","the edge of a finished path","tying back his hair","tying her apron","tying her shoe","tying his scarf","tying the bow","unfair","unfastened","unfolding the blanket","unpacked","washing her hands","washing the apples","watching the bird","waving a flag","waving to her friend","we","weighing the flour","weighing the puppy","wiping the bench","wiping the table","writing the card","zipping the bag",16,31,37,"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/dad-98c59a2436.mp3","A bucket caught the drips from the ceiling.","A model castle filled the classroom doorway. People bumped it when they entered. The builders moved it onto a side table, and people could walk through without touching it.","A visitor returned the lost mitten.","After using the magnifier, Sol left it in his coat. The nature group searched the shelf and could not start. Sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","Ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. She showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. The book returned to the shelf.","Bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. She carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. The whole set reached the hall together.","Eight pebbles filled the little wooden dish.","Eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. At rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. He liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","Five candles stood around the birthday cake.","Four toy trains waited on the station shelf.","Grandad tuned the violin before the concert.","Hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. A helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. Hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","Ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. His friend began looking for a loose window. Ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","Jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. They nearly bumped. Jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","Jun wrapped the drum in a blanket.","Lea took a ruler from Ben’s desk because he was outside. Ben returned and could not finish his chart. Next time Lea asked first, and Ben found a spare ruler for her.","Leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. Dad asked her to touch the soil. It was already wet. They moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","Mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. She looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. She put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","Milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. She had no chance to try a piece. He showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","My brother counted the spare buttons.","Nine stepping stones lay across the shallow stream.","Noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. The teacher fed them. The next day Noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","Oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. His group had none left. He returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","Purple fabric covered the puppet’s tiny stage.","Rafi clipped the photograph onto a string.","Rafi slid the note beneath the door.","Ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. He asked a helper to carry the other end. Together they moved it onto the trolley.","Rina carried the empty tray upstairs.","Seven flags lined the path to the hall.","Six empty baskets stood beside the fruit stall.","Spare batteries waited inside the drawer.","The baker sprinkled seeds over the loaf.","The broken mug held Mira’s paintbrushes.","The caretaker opened the side gate.","The class map hung beside the clock.","The coach left the cones by the fence.","The diver carried a camera beneath the water.","The gardener lifted the heavy stone.","The goalkeeper collected the orange bibs.","The group began a game without explaining it to a new child. She ran to the wrong end and stopped. They showed her the goal and played a slow round together before starting again.","The group decorated a cart while its loose wheel still wobbled. The cart could not carry their bags. They fixed the wheel first on the next cart, then added ribbons when it rolled properly.","The librarian repaired the torn poster.","The missing bead lay under the carpet.","The painted mask rested behind the curtain.","The silver badge stayed inside the jacket pocket.","The wet umbrella stood inside a tall vase.","Three skipping ropes hung above the shoe rack.","Three swimmers wore green caps.","Tom told a visitor that the hall was “over there.” The visitor chose the wrong door. Tom named the blue door beside the stairs, and the visitor found the hall.","Two builders pulled their cardboard bridge towards different tables. A joint came loose. They stopped, chose one place together and carried the bridge there side by side.","Two cushions lay inside the reading tent.","Two runners began from different lines. The nearer runner won, but nobody knew who was faster. They started again from one line and could compare their running.","Una coloured the blank part of her friend’s drawing to help. Her friend had wanted to leave it white for snow. On the next drawing Una asked what was needed and held the paper instead.","When Kim lost, she pushed the board and scattered the pieces. Her friend stopped playing. Kim helped set it up again and asked for another game without changing the old result.","bet","bucket","bud","bus","button","candle","cap","carpet","cat does not match the supplied spoken_medial_vowel_discrimination evidence.","construct_short_vowel_phoneme_sequence:short_i","dip","fair","fan","fed","flower","g","garden","gas","helicopter","hfw-word:can","hip","hum","jab","lab","lot","market","mitten"