 with their heavier loads.","a net","a new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. they showed her and practised a slow round. in class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. a partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","a pupil","a saucepan","a sheet","a teacher","a torch","a towel","a visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge. she had left her bag before pinning on the badge.","a visitor returned the lost mitten.","a visitor","a worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens. if a part is loose, she puts a barrier around that equipment. she writes the fault on a repair sheet for the repair team.","above the door","above the shoe rack","after using the magnifier, sol left it in his coat. the nature group searched the shelf and could not start. sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","all","an","are","as","at book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. they put books with missing pages aside. other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","at the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls. they tick each completed job on a chart. afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","at the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath. children can fill their bottles without tipping them sideways. spilled water runs through holes in a tray instead of collecting on the floor.","at the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan. readers can then borrow something else. the returned books go on labelled trolleys so another helper can take them to the right shelves.","at the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. families check it before going upstairs. a board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. she showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. the book returned to the shelf.","ava tore the cover of a shared book. she helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. he helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","back","bank","be","bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. at a display, ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. he made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. she carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. the whole set reached the hall together.","bea filled the jug after folding the napkins. she had chosen the dish before folding the napkins.","bed does not match the supplied spoken_medial_vowel_discrimination evidence.","before choosing a book, noor stacked the cushions. she had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","before choosing a pear, lina lifted her basket. she had counted her coins before lifting the basket.","before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. this makes it easy to find each amount when needed. after cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","before drying her shoes, tess folded the map. before folding the map, she counted the birds.","before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names. at each crossing she waits until the whole group is together. a helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","before packing his notebook, arun tied his scarf. before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","before photographing the jetty, finn put away his hat. before putting away his hat, he handed over his ticket.","before putting on his hat, eli sharpened his pencil. before sharpening the pencil, he had counted the butterflies.","before setting out the chairs, sal closed the window. before closing the window, sal had tested the microphone.","before waving to her friend, ada folded her scarf. before folding the scarf, she had checked the clock.","behind a low chair","behind the curtain","behind the desk","bell","beneath the coat hooks","beneath the jacket collar","beneath the stage","beside a small cupboard","beside the clock","beside the cushion","beside the jacket zip","beside the window","best","bike","brown paper","but","butterfly","by the door","by the fence","by","camera","carrying the hoop happens before checking the score, which happens before tying her shoe; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","checking the clock happens before folding her scarf, which happens before waving to her friend; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","chest","choosing a chair happens before putting on a coat, which happens before drawing the moon; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","choosing the dish happens before folding the napkins, which happens before filling the jug; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","clip","closing the drawer happened after checking the address. before checking the address, bo had sorted the cards.","closing the shade happens before filling the trough, which happens before counting the visitors; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","coach","coat does not match the supplied familiar_word_within_category evidence.","coloured","colourful","connected","corn","costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name. actors find the clothes for their own role there. a repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","counting her coins happens before lifting her basket, which happens before choosing a pear; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","counting the birds happens before folding the map, which happens before drying her shoes; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","counting the butterflies happens before sharpening his pencil, which happens before putting on his hat; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","counting the pots happens before opening the packet, which happens before drawing the labels; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","counting the tickets happened after tying the bow. before tying the bow, the helper had opened the tin.","crane","crossing the bridge happens before colouring the picture, which happens before drinking water; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","cup does not match the supplied familiar_word_within_category evidence.","dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat. he hung his coat after reading his ticket.","date","day","desk","did","dinosaur","do","drawing a line happens before folding the cloth, which happens before lifting the magnet; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat. before putting on the coat, may had chosen a chair.","eight pebbles filled the little wooden dish.","eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it. at music club, may rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. she tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","eli refused to move scenery because he had never done it. at rehearsal he tried moving one light panel with a partner. he liked helping the scene change and chose that job for the play.","eve put out the menus after wiping the table. she had moved the vase before wiping the table.","f","fairer","fastened","fetching the register happens before ringing the buzzer, which happens before hanging up the keys; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","five candles stood around the birthday cake.","flour","for","four toy trains waited on the station shelf.","get","gift","go","gorilla","grandad tuned the violin before the concert.","green leaves","guitar","had","hana left a tap dripping after filling a bowl. a helper showed her the growing puddle in the sink. hana closed the tap fully, and the dripping stopped.","hana left a tap dripping, then closed it fully when a helper showed her. at the craft table, bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. he took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","hand","handing over his ticket happens before putting away his hat, which happens before photographing the jetty; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","hanging up his helmet happens before rolling in the bike, which happens before folding the rag; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","harmed","harmful","has","he","helpers rinse empty food tubs before our model workshop. sticky food is removed so the tubs are ready to handle. they sort clean tubs, lids and cardboard into separate trays for the builders to choose from.","her","him","his","house","how","humming the song happened after opening the curtain. before opening the curtain, dad had put the bear on the bed.","if","inside a tall vase","inside the drawer","inside the jacket pocket","inside the shed","inside the slipper","inside the sports box","ivo blamed the wind after scattering the score cards. his friend looked for a loose window until ivo explained the spill. at a match, mae wrote an extra goal for her team. she told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","ivo scattered the score cards and said the wind had done it. his friend began looking for a loose window. ivo explained what had happened, and they put the cards back in order.","jem slid before the child below had moved away, and they nearly bumped. on his next turn he waited for a clear space. at music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. they agreed to play one short turn each.","jem started down the slide before the child below had moved away. they nearly bumped. jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","jo tied her shoe after checking the score. she had carried the hoop before checking the score.","jun wrapped the drum in a blanket.","kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. he had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket.","kangaroo","kettle","kim scattered the board after losing. she helped set it up and asked for another game without changing the result. a runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","labelled tubs separate deliveries for each classroom. a helper puts each parcel into the tub with its room number. another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","lamp","lamps light the path from the car park to our evening event. visitors can see uneven ground beneath their feet. at the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","lea took a ruler from ben’s desk because he was outside. ben returned and could not finish his chart. next time lea asked first, and ben found a spare ruler for her.","lea took ben’s ruler while he was outside, leaving him unable to finish his chart. next time she asked, and he found her a spare. otter used badger’s umbrella without asking. badger searched for it in the rain. later otter asked to borrow it and agreed when to return it.","leaving her bag happens before pinning on a badge, which happens before greeting the host; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","leila guessed that drooping leaves meant dry soil. touching the wet soil led her to move the plant from the hot sun instead. arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. a notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. he checked the rack and found his hat.","leila said a plant needed water because its leaves hung down. dad asked her to touch the soil. it was already wet. they moved the pot out of the hot sun instead, and the leaves lifted later.","letter","list","mara nearly recycled a plain bag because she thought it was empty. looking inside revealed the missing puppet shoes. at playtime, ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","mara thought the plain paper bag was empty and nearly recycled it. she looked inside and found the missing puppet shoes. she put the shoes with the puppet before recycling the empty bag.","match_spoken_short_vowel_word:short_e","may","measuring the card happens before clipping up the plan, which happens before finding the tape; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","microphone","milo kept finishing his sister’s puzzle for her. he began showing one useful move, then handing the pieces back. at music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. he offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","milo took over his sister’s puzzle whenever she paused. she had no chance to try a piece. he showed how to find an edge, then handed the pieces back and waited while she tried.","mina chose a spoon after tying her apron. she had washed the apples before tying her apron.","mock.v8.language.action.0.catch","mock.v8.language.action.0.climb","mock.v8.language.action.0.crawl","mock.v8.language.action.0.cry","mock.v8.language.action.0.dance","mock.v8.language.action.0.draw","mock.v8.language.action.0.eat","mock.v8.language.action.0.hug","mock.v8.language.action.0.laugh","mock.v8.language.action.0.point","mock.v8.language.action.0.pull","mock.v8.language.action.0.push","mock.v8.language.action.0.read","mock.v8.language.action.0.smile","mock.v8.language.action.0.sneeze","mock.v8.language.action.0.stretch","mock