tones lay across the shallow stream.","noor forgot her promised fish-feeding job while playing. the next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. for the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. the teacher fed them. the next day noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","now","of","oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. he returned the sheet and they divided them. at games club, may kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. his group had none left. he returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","on the shelf","one","opening the tin happens before tying the bow, which happens before counting the tickets; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","or","our class draws the sky and records the temperature each morning. each page has a date. on friday we lay the pages together to find which mornings were warmer and which had rain.","our picnic cart has deep sides to stop baskets slipping off. straps hold the drinks upright while it moves. its large wheels roll over the bumpy grass between the gate and our picnic spot.","out","overfilled","packed","packing her cup happens before watching the bird, which happens before zipping the bag; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","palm","pan","passing out the shakers happens before ringing the bell, which happens before moving the stool; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","patch","penguin","picture maps at the welcome desk show the rooms in our school. visitors can follow the marked route to a classroom. helpers also answer questions about lessons and clubs that are not shown on the maps.","pitch","post","pupil","pupils borrow instruments from the music cupboard. the teacher records each borrower’s name beside an instrument number. when an instrument comes back, a helper checks it and replaces worn strings before it is lent again.","purple fabric covered the puppet’s tiny stage.","purple fabric","putting the bear on the bed happens before opening the curtain, which happens before humming the song; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","r does not match the supplied first_letter evidence.","rafi clipped the photograph onto a string.","rafi slid the note beneath the door.","raisins","reading his ticket happens before hanging his coat, which happens before filling his bottle; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","reconnected","recounted","refastened","ren closed the atlas after stacking the cards. he had rotated the globe before stacking the cards.","ren could not lift a heavy crate alone, so he asked a helper to share its weight. tess promised to make twenty decorations in one evening but finished only two. for the next event she offered to make two, and the group divided the remaining work.","ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. he asked a helper to carry the other end. together they moved it onto the trolley.","repacked","rina carried the empty tray upstairs.","rock","rotating the globe happens before stacking the cards, which happens before closing the atlas; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","rug","see","seeds","seven flags lined the path to the hall.","sewing the puppet’s hat happens before moving the screen, which happens before closing the box; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","she","signs above the stairs show which platforms are below. travellers follow the number printed on their tickets. when a train changes platform, staff at the information desk explain the change and point out the new route.","six empty baskets stood beside the fruit stall.","small pockets keep pencils away from the books in our backpack. wide shoulder straps spread the weight while we carry it. a buckle lets us shorten the straps when the bag hangs too low.","so","sol left the magnifier in his coat, and the nature group could not find it. he returned it to its labelled shelf. hana put a game counter in a pencil tin by mistake. the next players lacked a counter until she put it back in the game box.","sol put his bag on the bench after reading the sign. reading the sign happened after he tied back his hair.","sorting the cards happens before checking the address, which happens before closing the drawer; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","spare batteries waited inside the drawer.","stroking the cat happens before stacking the cushions, which happens before choosing a book; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","taking a bow happens before moving the screen, which happens before stopping the fan; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","tent","testing the microphone happens before closing the window, which happens before setting out the chairs; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","the actors stopped the fan after moving the screen. moving the screen happened after they took a bow.","the baker sprinkled seeds over the loaf.","the baker wiped the bench after setting the timer. the timer was set after the flour was weighed.","the broken mug held mira’s paintbrushes.","the builder","the caretaker opened the side gate.","the class drew the labels after opening the packet. before opening the packet, they had counted the pots.","the class lifted the magnet after folding the cloth. before folding the cloth, they had drawn a line.","the class map hung beside the clock.","the coach left the cones by the fence.","the coin","the cyclist folded the rag after rolling in the bike. before rolling in the bike, he had hung up his helmet.","the diver carried a camera beneath the water.","the does not match the supplied spoken_to_print_high_frequency_word_recognition evidence.","the drawing","the driver","the gardener lifted the heavy stone.","the gardener","the goalkeeper collected the orange bibs.","the goalkeeper","the group began a game without explaining it to a new child. she ran to the wrong end and stopped. they showed her the goal and played a slow round together before starting again.","the group decorated a cart while its loose wheel still wobbled. the cart could not carry their bags. they fixed the wheel first on the next cart, then added ribbons when it rolled properly.","the group drank water after colouring the picture. they had crossed the bridge before colouring the picture.","the group found the tape after clipping up the plan. they had measured the card before clipping up the plan.","the keeper counted the visitors after filling the trough. before filling the trough, she closed the shade.","the librarian repaired the torn poster.","the librarian","the library van carries books on shelves with bars across the front. the bars hold the books in place during travel. every week the van stops at villages where readers cannot easily reach the town library.","the lunchbox has separate spaces for fruit and sandwiches. these stop soft food being squashed against the apples. two clips hold the lid shut when the lunchbox tips inside a school bag.","the missing bead lay under the carpet.","the note","the nurse moved the blanket after weighing the puppy. she had written the card before weighing the puppy.","the office records where and when each lost object was found. a label stays with the object. people looking for something describe it, and the office checks the description against the label before returning it.","the painted mask rested behind the curtain.","the painter","the players closed the box after moving the screen. they had moved the screen after sewing the puppet’s hat.","the postcard","the potter covered the clay after smoothing the bowl. smoothing the bowl happened after washing her hands.","the referee","the silver badge stayed inside the jacket pocket.","the teacher hung up the keys after ringing the buzzer. she had fetched the register before ringing the buzzer.","the teacher","the wet umbrella stood inside a tall vase.","three skipping ropes hung above the shoe rack.","three swimmers wore green caps.","tickets for our play show the row and seat for each visitor. helpers use the tickets to guide families into place. a printed programme names the characters and lists the scenes so families can follow the play.","tiger","tom told a visitor that the hall was “over there.” the visitor chose the wrong door. tom named the blue door beside the stairs, and the visitor found the hall.","tom’s “over there” sent a visitor to the wrong door. naming the blue door beside the stairs helped. mina sent a message asking for “the thing” from the cupboard. her partner brought the wrong object until mina asked for the red measuring jug on the lower shelf.","tub","two builders pulled a bridge towards different tables and loosened a joint. they chose one place together before carrying it. during a play, two children both began announcing the next scene. they paused, agreed which scenes each would announce and restarted without speaking over each other.","two builders pulled their cardboard bridge towards different tables. a joint came loose. they stopped, chose one place together and carried the bridge there side by side.","two cushions lay inside the reading tent.","two runners began from different lines. the nearer runner won, but nobody knew who was faster. they started again from one line and could compare their running.","two runners started from different lines, so their race did not show who was faster. they raced again from one line. bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. she used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","tying back his hair happens