d-b766971baf.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-bigger-bowl-instead-of-closing-a-dripping-tap-37beafbe45.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-an-absent-person-s-things-while-their-seat-is-empty-b3b36b6064.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-the-same-cup-when-comparing-how-much-jugs-hold-4da7b93730.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wait-beside-a-heavy-box-until-every-job-is-finished-b63e60d46a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wait-until-the-bottom-of-a-slide-is-clear-5d517e3bba.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wait-until-the-play-ends-before-trying-a-scenery-job-cb4fcedfb7.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/washing-her-hands-bd2d928a4a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/washing-the-apples-378c898008.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/watching-the-bird-d5a733bb8e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/waving-a-flag-512fa7afe6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/waving-to-her-friend-da8e0340e6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/weighing-the-flour-fa32d39dca.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/weighing-the-puppy-7ef6f05242.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wiping-the-bench-3d4b1aeb4e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wiping-the-table-db8036ce9b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/writing-the-card-3ba0e3bace.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/zipping-the-bag-4dc7aea2e1.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/a-camera-6c1fa2c1bf.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/a-torch-ef86ea783d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/above-the-door-a0274deda6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/gran-3d1d66baa8.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/harmful-d29d9701f9.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/harmless-e4161b659e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/inside-the-shed-d1a6220b83.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/the-gardener-17eaba6250.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/the-painter-6415a41631.mp3","/images/assessment/objective-words/jam.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/tent.webp","/images/child-mode/digraphs/chair.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/bus.webp","A board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due. People use it to decide whether to wait or walk. A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden. Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil. Classes open the gate when their visit begins.","A crane stood on long legs in the pond, spreading its wings before it flew away.","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it. For a birthday, Ari spent all his coins on wrapping paper and could not buy the card he needed. Next time he chose the card first and used the coins left over for wrapping paper.","A metal clip held the two sheets together so they did not blow away.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table. At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","A narrow footbridge lets walkers cross our river without waiting. It cannot carry vehicles. A ferry farther downstream has room for vans and takes them across with their heavier loads.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round. In class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. A partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","A tall palm had a ringed trunk and long leaves above the beach.","A visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge. She had left her bag before pinning on the badge.","A worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens. If a part is loose, she puts a barrier around that equipment. She writes the fault on a repair sheet for the repair team.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. They put books with missing pages aside. Other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","At the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls. They tick each completed job on a chart. Afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","At the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath. Children can fill their bottles without tipping them sideways. Spilled water runs through holes in a tray instead of collecting on the floor.","At the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan. Readers can then borrow something else. The returned books go on labelled trolleys so another helper can take them to the right shelves.","At the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. Families check it before going upstairs. A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","Ava tore the cover of a shared book. She helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. Leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. He helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","Bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","Bea filled the jug after folding the napkins. She had chosen the dish before folding the napkins.","Before choosing a book, Noor stacked the cushions. She had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","Before choosing a pear, Lina lifted her basket. She had counted her coins before lifting the basket.","Before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. This makes it easy to find each amount when needed. After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","Before drying her shoes, Tess folded the map. Before folding the map, she counted the birds.","Before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names. At each crossing she waits until the whole group is together. A helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","Before packing his notebook, Arun tied his scarf. Before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","Before photographing the jetty, Finn put away his hat. Before putting away his hat, he handed over his ticket.","Before putting on his hat, Eli sharpened his pencil. Before sharpening the pencil, he had counted the butterflies.","Before setting out the chairs, Sal closed the window. Before closing the window, Sal had tested the microphone.","Before waving to her friend, Ada folded her scarf. Before folding the scarf, she had checked the clock.","Closing the drawer happened after checking the address. Before checking the address, Bo had sorted the cards.","Costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name. Actors find the clothes for their own role there. A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","Counting the tickets happened after tying the bow. Before tying the bow, the helper had opened the tin.","Dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat. He hung his coat after reading his ticket.","Dad tapped the metal nail through the wooden board with a hammer.","Drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat. Before putting on the coat, May had chosen a chair.","Each pupil carried a schoolbook into the classroom and sat down for a lesson.","Eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it. At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","Eve put out the menus after wiping the table. She had moved the vase before wiping the table.","Hana left a tap dripping, then closed it fully when a helper showed her. At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","Helpers rinse empty food tubs before our model workshop. Sticky food is removed so the tubs are ready to handle. They sort clean tubs, lids and cardboard into separate trays for the builders to choose from.","Humming the song happened after opening the curtain. Before opening the curtain, Dad had put the bear on the bed.","Ivo blamed the wind after scattering the score cards. His friend looked for a loose window until Ivo explained the spill. At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","Jem slid before the child below had moved away, and they nearly bumped. On his next turn he waited for a clear space. At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","Jo counted the shells once, but her total was wrong. She had not counted them again.","Jo tied her shoe after checking the score. She had carried the hoop before checking the score.","Kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. He had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket.","Kim scattered the board after losing. She helped set it up and asked for another game without changing the result. A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","Kit zipped the bag after watching the bird. Watching the bird happened after she packed her cup.","Labelled tubs separate deliveries for each classroom. A helper puts each parcel into the tub with its room number. Another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","Lamps light the path from the car park to our evening event. Visitors can see uneven ground beneath their feet. At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","Lea took Ben’s ruler while he was outside, leaving him unable to finish his chart. Next time she asked, and he found her a spare. Otter used Badger’s umbrella without asking. Badger searched for it in the rain. Later Otter asked to borrow it and agreed when to return it.","Leila guessed that drooping leaves meant dry soil. Touching the wet soil led her to move the plant from the hot sun instead. Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","Lia emptied her bottle after a drink, then filled it a second time. She stopped exactly at the marked line, which showed the required amount.","Mara nearly recycled a plain bag because she thought it was empty. Looking inside revealed the missing puppet shoes. At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","Milo kept finishing his sister’s puzzle for her. He began showing one useful move, then handing the pieces back. At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","Mina chose a spoon after tying her apron. She had washed the apples before tying her apron.","Moving the stool happened after ringing the bell. Before ringing the bell, the children had passed out the shakers.","Mum stitched a cloth patch over the hole in my trousers.","Nia took every toy out of the box and left the toys loose on the mat. She put none back into the box.","Noor forgot her promised fish-feeding job while playing. The next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. Finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. For the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","Oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. He returned the sheet and they divided them. At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","Our bus sat in a traffic jam, with vehicles blocking the road ahead.","Our class draws the sky and records the temperature each morning. Each page has a date. On Friday we lay the pages together to find which mornings were warmer and which had rain.","Our picnic cart has deep sides to stop baskets slipping off. Straps hold the drinks upright while it moves. Its large wheels roll over the bumpy grass between the gate and our picnic spot.","Picture maps at the welcome desk show the rooms in our school. Visitors can follow the marked route to a classroom. Helpers also answer questions about lessons and clubs that are not shown on the maps.","Pupils borrow instruments from the music cupboard. The teacher records each borrower’s name beside an instrument number. When an instrument comes back, a helper checks it and replaces worn strings before it is lent again.","Ren closed the atlas after stacking the cards. He had rotated the globe before stacking the cards.","Ren could not lift a heavy crate alone, so he asked a helper to share its weight. Tess promised to make twenty decorations in one evening but finished only two. For the next event she offered to make two, and the group divided the remaining work.","Rock was piled beside the new path, with small stones ready for the builders.","Signs above the stairs show which platforms are below. Travellers follow the number printed on their tickets. When a train changes platform, staff at the information desk explain the change and point out the new route.","Small pockets keep pencils away from the books in our backpack. Wide shoulder straps spread the weight while we carry it. A buckle lets us shorten the straps when the bag hangs too low.","Sol left the magnifier in his coat, and the nature group could not find it. He returned it to its labelled shelf. Hana put a game counter in a pencil tin by mistake. The next players lacked a counter until she put it back in the game box.","Sol put his bag on the bench after reading the sign. Reading the sign happened after he tied back his hair.","The actors stopped the fan after moving the screen. Moving the screen happened after they took a bow.","The baker wiped the bench after setting the timer. The timer was set after the flour was weighed.","The clasp held Sara’s necklace closed. Sara opened the clasp and separated the two ends. She left the ends apart.","The class drew the labels after opening the packet. Before opening the packet, they had counted the pots.","The class lifted the magnet after folding the cloth. Before folding the cloth, they had drawn a line.","The clear sheet had no colour. It was not tinted red, blue or any other colour.","The coach showed the team how to pass the ball and planned their practice.","The cyclist folded the rag after rolling in the bike. Before rolling in the bike, he had hung up his helmet.","The date on the invitation was the day of our party.","The edge was covered in soft foam. It could not hurt a child who bumped it, and the edge itself was not damaged.","The fan beside the desk spun its blades and blew air across the warm room.","The group drank water after colouring the picture. They had crossed the bridge before colouring the picture.","The group found the tape after clipping up the plan. They had measured the card before clipping up the plan.","The juice leaked until Mina twisted the cap tightly onto the bottle.","The keeper counted the visitors after filling the trough. Before filling the trough, she closed the shade.","The letter arrived in an envelope with news from Gran.","The library van carries books on shelves with bars across the front. The bars hold the books in place during travel. Every week the van stops at villages where readers cannot easily reach the town library.","The lunchbox has separate spaces for fruit and sandwiches. These stop soft food being squashed against the apples. Two clips hold the lid shut when the lunchbox tips inside a school bag.","The nurse moved the blanket after weighing the puppy. She had written the card before weighing the puppy.","The office records where and when each lost object was found. A label stays with the object. People looking for something describe it, and the office checks the description against the label before returning it.","The players closed the box after moving the screen. They had moved the screen after sewing the puppet’s hat.","The players ran onto the grassy pitch and placed the ball between the goals.","The plug had joined the lamp to the socket. An adult pulled it out and left it lying on the table. Nobody put it back.","The post arrived in a bag of letters that the carrier left at our door.","The potter covered the clay after smoothing the bowl. Smoothing the bowl happened after washing her hands.","The rules gave every player one turn. Only one child was given extra turns because he was the leader’s friend. This did not make the turns more equal.","The teacher hung up the keys after ringing the buzzer. She had fetched the register before ringing the buzzer.","The wooden chest had a hinged lid, with blankets stored inside.","Tickets for our play show the row and seat for each visitor. Helpers use the tickets to guide families into place. A printed programme names the characters and lists the scenes so families can follow the play.","Tom’s “over there” sent a visitor to the wrong door. Naming the blue door beside the stairs helped. Mina sent a message asking for “the thing” from the cupboard. Her partner brought the wrong object until Mina asked for the red measuring jug on the lower shelf.","Two builders pulled a bridge towards different tables and loosened a joint. They chose one place together before carrying it. During a play, two children both began announcing the next scene. They paused, agreed which scenes each would announce and restarted without speaking over each other.","Two runners started from different lines, so their race did not show who was faster. They raced again from one line. Bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. She used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","Una coloured a blank space that her friend wanted to leave white for snow. Next time she asked and held the paper instead. Dad moved a model to tidy the table, but its maker was still arranging it. On the next visit he asked which part of the table could be cleared.","a does not match the supplied first_letter evidence.","a does not match the supplied last_letter evidence.","apple does not match the supplied familiar_word_within_category evidence.","bed does not match the supplied familiar_word_within_category evidence.","bowl does not match the supplied familiar_word_within_category evidence.","c","construct_short_vowel_phoneme_sequence:short_o","construct_short_vowel_phoneme_sequence:short_u","hfw-word:all","hfw-word:an","hfw-word:and","hfw-word:are","hfw-word:as","hfw-word:be","hfw-word:but","hfw-word:by","hfw-word:day","hfw-word:did","hfw-word:do","hfw-word:for","hfw-word:get","hfw-word:go","hfw-word:had","hfw-word:has","hfw-word:he","hfw-word:her","hfw-word:him","hfw-word:his","hfw-word:how","hfw-word:if","hfw-word:may","hfw-word:my","hfw-word:no","hfw-word:not","hfw-word:now","hfw-word:of","hfw-word:one","hfw-word:or","hfw-word:out","hfw-word:see","hfw-word:she","hfw-word:so","hfw-word:the","hfw-word:two","hfw-word:up","hfw-word:use","hfw-word:was","hfw-word:way","hfw-word:we","hfw-word:who","hfw-word:you","j","leg","log","match_spoken_short_vowel_word:short_i","mock-foundation-word:belt","mock.v8.comp