n-US/supplemental/tip-27fdea1a44.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/use-99bcbb9c6c.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/vulture-ca5632392f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/watermelon-d3fb20877f.mp3","A bear sleeps through winter.","A board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due.","A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden.","A crane stood on long legs in the pond, spreading its wings before it flew away. Across the road, a building crane lifted steel beams with a long arm and hook.","A ferry farther downstream has room for vans and takes them across with their heavier loads.","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it.","A helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","A lantern lit the dark path.","A metal clip held the two sheets together so they did not blow away. On her tablet, Mina played a short clip that showed a bird taking off, then stopped after a few seconds.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table.","A mouse nibbles a seed.","A narrow footbridge lets walkers cross our river without waiting.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round.","A printed programme names the characters and lists the scenes so families can follow the play.","A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","A tall palm had a ringed trunk and long leaves above the beach. Jo held a shell on her open palm, between her fingers and her wrist.","A truck carries the heavy boxes.","A visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge.","A wooden post held up one end of the fence. Later, the post arrived in a bag of letters that the carrier left at our door.","A worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Acts on the original guess even though the soil is already wet.","Acts on the untested guess and risks discarding the puppet shoes.","Adds a load before correcting the fault that prevents the cart carrying it.","Adds speed without settling the disagreement about where the bridge should go.","After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","After running, I could feel my heart beating inside my chest. I sat beside a wooden chest with a hinged lid and blankets inside.","Afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","Agree on a plan before working together. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Agree on a plan before working together. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil.","An elephant has a long trunk.","Another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading.","At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","At the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls.","At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","At the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath.","At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","At the named occurrence, cap means a cover that closes a bottle.","At the named occurrence, chest means a storage box with a lid.","At the named occurrence, clip means a small fastener that holds things together.","At the named occurrence, coach means a person who trains a team.","At the named occurrence, crane means a long-legged bird.","At the named occurrence, date means a particular day on a calendar.","At the named occurrence, fan means a machine that moves air.","At the named occurrence, jam means a line of traffic that cannot move freely.","At the named occurrence, letter means a written message sent to someone.","At the named occurrence, nail means a metal fastener for wood.","At the named occurrence, palm means a kind of tree.","At the named occurrence, patch means a piece of material covering a hole.","At the named occurrence, pitch means a field where a game is played.","At the named occurrence, post means letters delivered to a home.","At the named occurrence, pupil means a learner at a school.","At the named occurrence, rock means a solid stone material.","At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","At the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan.","At the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses.","Ava tore the cover of a shared book. She helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it.","Avoids the activity instead of correcting the misplaced tool that caused the problem.","Bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it.","Bea filled the jug after folding the napkins.","Bea measured how much two jugs held by filling them with cupfuls, but she used different-sized cups. She used the same cup for both jugs and counted the cupfuls again.","Before checking the address, Bo had sorted the cards.","Before choosing a book, Noor stacked the cushions.","Before choosing a pear, Lina lifted her basket.","Before closing the window, Sal had tested the microphone.","Before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls.","Before drying her shoes, Tess folded the map.","Before filling the trough, she closed the shade.","Before folding the cloth, they had drawn a line.","Before folding the map, she counted the birds.","Before folding the scarf, she had checked the clock.","Before opening the curtain, Dad had put the bear on the bed.","Before opening the packet, they had counted the pots.","Before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names.","Before packing his notebook, Arun tied his scarf.","Before photographing the jetty, Finn put away his hat.","Before putting away his hat, he handed over his ticket.","Before putting on his hat, Eli sharpened his pencil.","Before putting on the coat, May had chosen a chair.","Before ringing the bell, the children had passed out the shakers.","Before rolling in the bike, he had hung up his helmet.","Before setting out the chairs, Sal closed the window.","Before sharpening the pencil, he had counted the butterflies.","Before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","Before tying the bow, the helper had opened the tin.","Before waving to her friend, Ada folded her scarf.","Changes decoration instead of fixing the wheel that prevents the cart working.","Changes the bowl without stopping the water that continues to drip.","Changes the pace without explaining the goal that the newcomer did not know.","Changes the route without reducing or sharing the weight that Ren could not lift.","Changes the slide rather than the waiting behaviour that prevented the bump.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Check what is true before acting on a guess. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Closing the drawer happened after checking the address.","Coloured describes something with colour or tint; the passage excludes any colour.","Colourful describes something with strong or varied colours; the sheet has none.","Conceals the tear instead of helping restore the shared book.","Confuses an owner’s absence with permission; Ben still needed his ruler.","Confuses choosing first with having a fair share; the other makers still need stickers.","Confuses moving quickly with having a clear space; the other child has not moved away.","Confuses visibility with access; a taller castle still occupies the doorway.","Connected would mean the plug still joins lamp and socket, but it is on the table.","Continues the search for an unrelated cause instead of explaining the known spill.","Costumes hang on rails labelled with each actor’s name.","Counting the tickets happened after tying the bow.","Dad filled his bottle after hanging his coat.","Dad moved a model to tidy the table, but its maker was still arranging it. On the next visit he asked which part of the table could be cleared.","Delays the trial until it can no longer help the current performance.","Dis- reverses connected: the plug no longer joins the lamp to the socket.","Drawing the moon happened after putting on a coat.","During a play, two children both began announcing the next scene. They paused, agreed which scenes each would announce and restarted without speaking over each other.","Eli pointed to the first letter in his printed name. Then he opened a letter from Gran and read the news she had written.","Eli refused an unfamiliar scenery job, then tried moving one panel with a partner and enjoyed it.","Ends play because another person won, rather than responding kindly to the result.","Eve put out the menus after wiping the table.","Every week the van stops at villages where readers ca